cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
type: software
title: "LSA Beamformer Reproduction"
abstract: >-
  An independent, documented Python implementation of the conventional
  mixed-directivity linear superarray (LSA) beamformer of Huang and Habets
  (EUSIPCO 2025), with verification checks, evaluation of Directivity Factor
  and White Noise Gain, and documentation of every convention needed to
  reproduce the results.
authors:
  - family-names: Qosimov
    given-names: Hamrozjon
    affiliation: "UWC ISAK Japan"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add if you have one
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/lsa-beamformer-reproduction"  # replace YOUR-USERNAME
keywords:
  - microphone arrays
  - beamforming
  - differential beamforming
  - linear superarray
  - directivity factor
  - white noise gain
  - reproducibility
